 nodes = case['nodes']\n    threshold = case['utility_threshold']\n    node_dict = {node['id']: node for node in nodes}\n    children = {node['id']: [] for node in nodes}\n    for node in nodes:\n        pid = node['parent']\n        if pid is not None:\n            children[pid].append(node['id'])\n    # Initialize queue: descending depth, then id\n    from collections import deque\n    all_ids = list(node_dict.keys())\n    all_ids.sort(key=lambda x: (-node_dict[x]['depth'], x))\n    queue = deque(all_ids)\n    queued = set(all_ids)\n    removed = set()\n    visit_order = []\n    while queue:\n        nid = queue.popleft()\n        queued.discard(nid)\n        if nid in removed:\n            continue\n        visit_order.append(nid)\n        node = node_dict[nid]\n        # Check if leaf\n        if len(children.get(nid, [])) == 0 and node['removable'] and node['utility'] <= threshold:\n            # Remove\n            removed.add(nid)\n            pid = node['parent']\n            if pid is not None and pid in children:\n                children[pid].remove(nid)\n                # Enqueue parent if not already in queue and not removed\n                if pid not in removed and pid not in queued:\n                    queue.append(pid)\n                    queued.add(pid)\n    # retained node ids in original order\n    retained = [n['id'] for n in nodes if n['id'] not in removed]\n    return {\"retained_node_ids\": retained, \"visit_order\": visit_order}\n\nWe should test on given fixture. It seems correct.\n\nNow wrap in JSON with key \"implementation\".\n\nNote: The code uses 'removable' as boolean, but in JSON it's true/false. Python's JSON parsing will give bool. So condition works.\n\nAlso note: The children dict initially contains all nodes, but when we remove a node, we also need to consider that the parent might not be in children? All nodes are in children dict initially. When we remove a child, we do children[pid].remove(nid). That's fine.\n\nPotential is